WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations, you guys.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.203 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Four fantastic seasons.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:06.373
As I told you both backstage, my
wife and I binged season four.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.307 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You nailed the landing.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's amazing
how you guys met.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.844 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You met on Twitter.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-We did.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:14.080
-And it's really one of the few
nice things that I feel like

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.716 size:84% position:42%
has come out of Twitter
is this wonderful show.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that's possibly
very true.

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it doesn't seem like
there's any competition lately

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
for good things that have
happened on Twitter.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:25.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We met when Twitter was nice,
right?

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.026 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:29.662
And Sharon was already
an incandescent star in the U.K.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but not yet here.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.931 line:92%
And I had seen a show of hers,

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I just love
British comedy,

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:38.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I wrote her a DM,
and I said, "Listen, listen,

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.142
I like you, and I'd like
to know you in real life."

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:46.913
And you sent a cease and desist
letter, which I ignored,

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:51.051
and then we met for lunch
almost 10 years ago now.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then decided to write
a script together.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:57.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had experience doing this.
You did not.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.391 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Correct.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:02.062
-So you really -- you really
sold her quite a bill of goods.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did indeed.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:06.266
I mean, I had done, you know --
I'd written jokes and done

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
lots of stand-up
and I'd written failed pilots

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:09.836 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and things like that.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Books. You'd written books.
-Oh, I'd written a book.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you could write.
Yeah, so you could do that.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your diary.
You're a big diary writer.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:19.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I have a diary, yeah.
-Your blog.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:19.846 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It just went online.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.581 size:84% position:42%
-I'm sure when you go
shopping for groceries,

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
you write down a few things.
-Yes, yes, thank you.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.486
So I felt prepared to write
a global sensation sitcom

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is now broadcast
in 130 countries. Thank you.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.290 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-130. That's amazing.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know
if there are 130 countries.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:35.228
I have to look at the --
that's what they told me.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it's 132.
-Wow.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I assume there's more.
-More coming.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.101
And then what was it like there
the first time

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:41.868 line:92%
you sat down to collaborate?

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.903
Because obviously you liked each
other's style on social media.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.439
But that's a different thing
when you're in a room writing.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:50.043 line:92%
-It was like a weird first date.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That you had to work at.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.780
It was like a date where
you decide to break the ice

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
by writing a sitcom about
the difficulties of marriage.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:57.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Deeply personal stuff.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Imagine if we knew each other
really well

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.821 size:84% position:42%
and we're going through
incredible difficulty

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.858
instead of just being new pals
who just met three minutes ago.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was weird and awkward,
but you get over it.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's weird writing --
or it's uncomfortable

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
writing comedy with someone,
anyway,

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you got to really put
yourself on the line

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be prepared
to say funny stuff

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.872
and not have anyone laugh at it.
-Yeah.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the other hard part
is being the person

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.009 size:75% position:38%
who then has to say,
"I don't like that."

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.545
-That is also hard.
-That's not easy, either. Yeah.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.347 size:81% position:41%
-I found out that --
you had a hard time --

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:30.083
We used to write it when we
lived in different countries.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When we would write remotely
and Sharon would be like,

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm not sure if we should do
this part," I'd be like,

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, really?"
I would yell at my computer.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you know how e-mail
always sounds worse.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:39.692 line:92%
But we're in the same room.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
If she was like, "What if
we did it this way?"

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.363
I'd be like,
"That's a super idea, partner."

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:47.300
But with e-mail, I'd throw
the laptop under the bus.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For those who don't know,
you were on business.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.605
You're basically an American man
on business in London,

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:55.175
you guys have a one-night stand,
you get pregnant.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One-week stand.
-One-week stand. That's right.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.879
And then you decide to --
when you get pregnant,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
you decide to move to London
and have the baby.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.517 line:92%
I will say there's a lot of --

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's like a married couple
making it work.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.822
Sounds like 80% of all sitcoms,
but yet you guys manage to avoid

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:13.126
most of the sitcom tropes that
I feel like people fall into.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:16.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were there ones you were
particularly trying to avoid?

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yeah.
We'd seen a lot of sitcoms

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:21.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the husband was like,
"Bam! Football!"

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.737
And where the wife was like,
"Yeah," with the ironing thing.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the ironing thing.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.574 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:29.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so we didn't
want to do that

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we're both married
in real life

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
and being married
is fascinating.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
It isn't boring.
It isn't, like, "Ugh."

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.450
It's like you want to kill
each other with a hammer

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.120
or you're hugging each other
around the ankles being like,

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.422 line:92%
"I can't believe you love me."

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so you spend more time
at those poles

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
than you do in the middle.
Be like, "Buh!"

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:48.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.396
That was not a dig at Al Bundy.
I love him.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you know what I mean?
-Sure.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:54.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We want to show
what it really felt like.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that was our goal.
-Yeah.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's basic things
we didn't want in there.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, we didn't want it
to be sentimental.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we didn't really say,
"I love you."

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:03.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Except for maybe one.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
Out of the whole four seasons,
I think we said --

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.648
-We were allowed to show
that they loved each other

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:09.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
but never say.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:13.486
-There was no cute kids.
I mean, there's kids in it.

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.554 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And they are cute.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're grand.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:19.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
We didn't want to give them
any lines.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.526 line:92%
-Yeah, they're not precocious.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We wouldn't know how to
write that, anyway.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:25.331
-And there's lots of good
sitcoms already being made

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:29.335
where the kid's like, "I put
peanut butter in the toaster."

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:29.836 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we figured that those
sitcoms are already out there.

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:35.375
We'll just do -- We will show
a relationship under the stress

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
of having kids, but we don't
need to, you know --

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there's no --
no loving sex.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.880 line:92%
There's no nice-looking sex.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.783 size:88% position:44%
There's no sex where we
look like we're in love.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:44.784 line:92%
It's just like, you know --

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:47.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's always like,
"Guess we got to do this."

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hurried.
-Very negotiated.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:53.526
-I would say when my wife and I
watch it and, you know, again,

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:56.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's half an hour, we,
like, side-eye each other,

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:59.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
like seven times
an episode because --

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-Yeah.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her favorite thing that ever
happened in an episode

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:05.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
is I believe the dog has died.
-Yes.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you're upset.
And you ask,

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Are you're upset
because the dog has died?"

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:10.610 size:88% position:44%
And you're upset because
the guests won't leave.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Won't leave.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That hit my wife more
in her core than anything.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.650
And me -- spoiler alert --
because in the upcoming season,

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:23.122
you eat a -- like, a yogurt
and then you get mad at him

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's the kid's food.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:28.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you scream
that it's not the kid's food

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:30.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you paid for it.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm not gonna lie.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:34.400
That's a conversation that,
maybe not in those exact words,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's happened in
the Meyers family household.

